      <h1>Sources and further reading</h1>
      <p>Technical standards and learning resources behind the research, organized for deeper study.</p>
    </header>
    <section aria-labelledby="standards"><h2 id="standards">Primary standards</h2><p>Numbered citations on the topic pages link to these entries. RFCs provide the technical basis, while the original Assignment 1 research supplies the starting structure.</p>
      <ol>
        <li id="rfc1945"><strong>[1] HTTP/1.0</strong><p>Berners-Lee, T., Fielding, R., &amp; Frystyk, H. (1996). <cite>Hypertext Transfer Protocol — HTTP/1.0</cite>. RFC 1945.</p><a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc1945.html">Read RFC 1945 ↗</a><p class="source-note">Useful for the early protocol and the HTTP/1.0 message model.</p></li>
        <li id="rfc9112"><strong>[2] HTTP/1.1</strong><p>Fielding, R., Nottingham, M., &amp; Reschke, J. (Eds.). (2022). <cite>HTTP/1.1</cite>. RFC 9112.</p><a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9112.html">Read RFC 9112 ↗</a><p class="source-note">Explains message framing and connection management.</p></li>
        <li id="rfc9113"><strong>[3] HTTP/2</strong><p>Thomson, M., &amp; Benfield, C. (Eds.). (2022). <cite>HTTP/2</cite>. RFC 9113.</p><a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9113.html">Read RFC 9113 ↗</a><p class="source-note">The current HTTP/2 specification, including framing and streams.</p></li>
        <li id="rfc9114"><strong>[4] HTTP/3</strong><p>Bishop, M. (Ed.). (2022). <cite>HTTP/3</cite>. RFC 9114.</p><a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114.html">Read RFC 9114 ↗</a><p class="source-note">Explains the mapping of HTTP onto QUIC.</p></li>
        <li id="rfc9110"><strong>[5] HTTP semantics</strong><p>Fielding, R., Nottingham, M., &amp; Reschke, J. (Eds.). (2022). <cite>HTTP Semantics</cite>. RFC 9110.</p><a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html">Read RFC 9110 ↗</a><p class="source-note">Shared meanings of methods, fields, status codes, and URI schemes.</p></li>
        <li id="rfc8446"><strong>[6] TLS 1.3</strong><p>Rescorla, E. (2018). <cite>The Transport Layer Security (TLS) Protocol Version 1.3</cite>. RFC 8446.</p><a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446.html">Read RFC 8446 ↗</a><p class="source-note">The technical foundation for the TLS discussion.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="learning"><h2 id="learning">Learning resources</h2><ul><li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP">MDN: HTTP overview</a> — explanations of requests, responses, and everyday HTTP behavior.</li><li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Guides/Evolution_of_HTTP">MDN: Evolution of HTTP</a> — a readable historical overview.</li><li><a href="https://ksuweb.github.io/IT3203/">IT 3203 class website</a> — course information and web development resources.</li></ul><p class="source-note">Research adapted from Deborah Daramola’s <cite>The Evolution of HTTP and HTTPS</cite>, Assignment 1, Fall 2026. Illustrations are original explanatory diagrams. External references checked October 17, 2026.</p></section>
